  <script>
    // Wallet and Car & license switch in-page state rather than navigating,
    // so they ride in the bar as `extra` buttons. The module below binds the
    // handlers by id once its render functions exist.
    if (window.SS_APPBAR) SS_APPBAR.mount({
      active: 'driving', id: 'consoleNav', startHidden: true,
      extra: [
        // Calls through window so it works on whichever bar instance is live:
        // ensure() swaps the signed-out bar for the signed-in one after the
        // in-page OTP sign-in, and a listener bound by id at parse time would
        // be on the bar that got removed (bug scan 2026-09-06).
        { label: 'Wallet', id: 'navWallet', onClick: function () { if (window.__ssRenderWallet) window.__ssRenderWallet(); } },
        // Car & license now lives under the avatar menu ("Vehicles & license"
        // → /cars) and on the Profile & account page (Justin, 2026-09-04).
      ],
    });
  </script>
  <script src="/js/ss-stops.js"></script>
  <script type="module">
    // driving.html - DRIVER web console, everything AFTER "your ride is posted".
    //
    // /driving                          -> the driver's rides
    // /driving?ride=<id>                -> one ride: requests, riders, check-in, complete
    // /driving?ride=<id>&chat=<bookingId> -> chat with one rider
    //
    // WHY this page exists: /post (built 2026-08-21) lets a driver post from a
    // browser, but every action AFTER a rider appears - accept, decline, chat,
    // check riders in, mark complete - lived only in the app. An app-less
    // driver's pending requests rotted until the card hold expired. This page
    // closes that loop.
    //
    // THE CONTRACT: services/bookings.ts is the source of truth for every
    // action here. Each handler below mirrors its app twin - the same server
    // call, the same conditional status guard, and the SAME follow-up side
    // effects (push + email + chat + Stripe hold release), because skipping a
    // follow-up means a rider who is never told they were accepted. File/line
    // references are inline at each handler.
    //
    // ONE hard rule throughout (same as trips.html): every value that came out
